Design only. It answers issue #167 and fixes the contract that #168-#174 must implement. The rule of this ADR: every behavior is
the Apache Pekko Classic behavior, traced to its source, its tests or a reproduction against the pinned runtime; a Go adaptation
keeps the observable behavior; a deviation or a Go-specific choice is listed for owner approval; a postponed capability is an
explicit gap and is never replaced by another behavior called parity. Nothing is decided here by what Verimand might need.

Two names are kept apart: **"ADR 0010 D3"** is the recommendation "default supervision: Restart (classic)" (`0010:225`);
**"the stop-on-failure divergence"** is today's behavior, where a failing actor stops (`docs/actor-core-parity.md:67,194`, ADR 0014
deviation 10 `:66`).

